## Component-Type Guidance

{% if component_type == 'navbar' or component_type == 'navigation' %}
- Keep navigation items clearly visible and accessible
- Include a mobile hamburger menu for responsive behavior
- Ensure the logo/brand mark is prominent and links to the homepage
- Use sticky/fixed positioning so the navbar remains visible on scroll
- Highlight the active page link with a visual indicator
- Place the primary CTA (e.g., "Sign Up", "Get Started") on the right side with a contrasting button style
- Ensure dropdown menus (if any) are keyboard-navigable
{% elif component_type == 'hero' %}
- Create strong visual impact with a clear value proposition
- Place the primary CTA above the fold with high contrast
- Use a compelling headline (H1) with a supporting subheadline
- Include social proof elements if available (e.g., customer count, ratings)
- Ensure the hero image or background does not reduce text readability
- Add adequate padding and whitespace to let the message breathe
{% elif component_type == 'footer' %}
- Organize links into logical columns (Product, Company, Resources, Legal)
- Include contact information and social media links
- Add a newsletter signup form if appropriate
- Keep the copyright notice and legal links at the very bottom
- Use a muted background color to visually separate from main content
- Ensure all links have adequate spacing for touch targets on mobile
{% elif component_type == 'sidebar' %}
- Maintain a clear visual hierarchy with section headings
- Use collapsible sections for long lists of links or filters
- Ensure the sidebar does not compete visually with main content
- Make it sticky on desktop so it stays in view while scrolling
- Hide or convert to a drawer/overlay on mobile breakpoints
{% elif component_type == 'card' or component_type == 'cards' %}
- Use consistent card dimensions and spacing within a grid
- Include a clear visual focal point (image, icon, or color accent)
- Keep card content concise: heading, short description, CTA
- Add hover/focus states for interactive cards
- Ensure cards stack vertically on mobile
{% elif component_type == 'form' %}
- Group related fields logically with clear labels
- Use inline validation and helpful error messages
- Make the submit button prominent and descriptive (not just "Submit")
- Ensure proper tab order and keyboard accessibility
- Add placeholder text only as supplementary hints, not as labels
{% elif component_type == 'header' %}
- Establish clear visual hierarchy with the page or section title
- Include breadcrumbs or contextual navigation if appropriate
- Use brand colors consistently
- Ensure adequate contrast between text and background
{% elif component_type == 'cta' or component_type == 'call-to-action' %}
- Use a contrasting button color that stands out from surrounding content
- Write action-oriented button text (e.g., "Start Free Trial" not "Click Here")
- Add urgency or benefit-driven supporting text
- Ensure the CTA is large enough for easy tapping on mobile
- Surround with whitespace to draw the eye
{% elif component_type == 'testimonial' or component_type == 'testimonials' %}
- Include author photos, names, and titles/companies for credibility
- Add star ratings or score indicators where applicable
- Use quotation styling to visually distinguish testimonial text
- Rotate or display multiple testimonials if content is available
{% else %}
- Follow general best practices for this component type
- Ensure clear visual hierarchy and consistent spacing
- Use the brand color palette effectively
- Make the component responsive across all breakpoints
{% endif %}

## Requirements
1. Preserve all existing content exactly -- do not invent or remove text
2. Use Tailwind CSS utility classes for all styling
3. The component must work both as a standalone snippet and when embedded inside a full page layout
4. Apply the brand color palette using Tailwind's arbitrary value syntax (e.g., `bg-[{{ primary_color }}]`) or closest Tailwind color classes
5. Ensure the component is fully responsive (mobile-first approach)
6. Include appropriate hover and focus states for interactive elements
7. Use semantic HTML elements (nav, header, footer, section, article, etc.)
8. Ensure color contrast meets WCAG AA standards

